 "captions": [
  [
   0.0,
   0.872,
   "Part two."
  ],
  [
   0.872,
   1.743,
   "Classical vision."
  ],
  [
   2.375,
   4.554,
   "Long before neural networks existed,"
  ],
  [
   4.554,
   8.041,
   "engineers crossed the semantic gap by hand\n\u2014"
  ],
  [
   8.041,
   9.784,
   "with clever mathematical filters."
  ],
  [
   10.416,
   13.031,
   "These old ideas are not obsolete."
  ],
  [
   13.031,
   16.518,
   "They are the bedrock that everything\nmodern is"
  ],
  [
   16.518,
   17.389,
   "built on."
  ],
  [
   18.021,
   21.508,
   "So let's roll up our sleeves and see"
  ],
  [
   21.508,
   23.251,
   "how they actually work."
  ],
  [
   23.751,
   26.9,
   "The most basic operation in all of vision"
  ],
  [
   26.9,
   28.08,
   "is the filter."
  ],
  [
   28.712,
   31.861,
   "A filter takes an image and transforms its"
  ],
  [
   31.861,
   33.829,
   "numbers to reveal something useful."
  ],
  [
   34.46,
   37.609,
   "Some filters are simple and work one pixel"
  ],
  [
   37.609,
   38.789,
   "at a time."
  ],
  [
   39.421,
   41.389,
   "To make an image brighter,"
  ],
  [
   41.389,
   44.538,
   "just add a fixed value to every pixel."
  ],
  [
   44.538,
   47.686,
   "Watch the numbers on the grid climb\ntogether."
  ],
  [
   48.318,
   49.499,
   "To increase contrast,"
  ],
  [
   49.499,
   52.647,
   "push the bright pixels brighter and the\ndark"
  ],
  [
   52.647,
   53.434,
   "pixels darker,"
  ],
  [
   53.434,
   54.615,
   "pulling them apart."
  ],
  [
   55.247,
   58.395,
   "But the truly interesting filters do\nsomething different."
  ],
  [
   58.395,
   60.757,
   "They look at a pixel's neighborhood,"
  ],
  [
   60.757,
   62.725,
   "not just the pixel itself."
  ],
  [
   63.356,
   64.143,
   "Take blur."
  ],
  [
   64.775,
   66.349,
   "To blur a pixel,"
  ],
  [
   66.349,
   69.498,
   "you replace it with the average of the"
  ],
  [
   69.498,
   71.072,
   "pixels immediately around it."
  ],
  [
   71.704,
   73.672,
   "Do that for every pixel,"
  ],
  [
   73.672,
   75.246,
   "and sharp edges soften."
  ],
  [
   75.878,
   76.271,
   "Now,"
  ],
  [
   76.271,
   79.026,
   "why would anyone want a blurry image?"
  ],
  [
   79.658,
   82.807,
   "Because blur removes noise \u2014 those tiny\nrandom"
  ],
  [
   82.807,
   85.955,
   "speckles a camera sensor adds in low\nlight."
  ],
  [
   86.587,
   89.736,
   "Averaging a neighborhood cancels the\nrandom flecks while"
  ],
  [
   89.736,
   91.31,
   "keeping the real shapes."
  ],
  [
   91.941,
   95.09,
   "And here is the insight that this whole"
  ],
  [
   95.09,
   96.271,
   "course turns on."
  ],
  [
   96.902,
   100.051,
   "This one little move \u2014 slide a small"
  ],
  [
   100.051,
   101.625,
   "window across the image,"
  ],
  [
   101.625,
   104.774,
   "and combine each neighborhood into a new\nvalue"
  ],
  [
   104.774,
   107.923,
   "\u2014 is the single most important idea in"
  ],
  [
   107.923,
   108.71,
   "computer vision."
  ],
  [
   109.341,
   111.309,
   "It has a formal name."
  ],
  [
   111.309,
   111.703,
   "Convolution."
  ],
  [
   112.334,
   115.483,
   "And it is so important that it deserves"
  ],
  [
   115.483,
   117.451,
   "a chapter entirely to itself."
  ]
 ],
